# Core Constraints

These rules apply to ALL work on InfinityQube. For game-specific architecture rules, see `game-architecture.mdc`.

## NEVER DO

### Architecture (see game-architecture.mdc)
- NEVER split core managers (Grid, Wave, Stage, Player, CubeCollision) without approval
- NEVER bypass `CubeCollisionManager` for collision logic
- NEVER violate Infinity immutability (only Infinity affects Infinity)
- NEVER scatter marker-to-cube conversion logic (keep in PlayerMarkerSystem)
- NEVER calculate grid positions manually (use GridManager methods)

### Code Safety
- NEVER use `FindFirstObjectByType<>()` in Update() or frequently called methods
- NEVER introduce new singleton patterns without approval
- NEVER modify `Assets/scripts/Utils/Enumerations.cs` without approval
- NEVER change Unity lifecycle patterns (Awake, Start, Update sequences)
- NEVER commit partial method implementations or incomplete control structures
- NEVER remove debug logging from critical operations

### Performance
- NEVER create unbounded loops without exit conditions
- NEVER allocate large arrays in frequently called methods
- NEVER use reflection in gameplay code
- NEVER use LINQ with allocation in hot paths

### Documentation
- NEVER create new documentation files without approval
- NEVER include technical implementation details in Project Doc files

## ALWAYS DO

### Before Changes
- ALWAYS check file size limits: Core (750), Managers (600), Utilities (300), Data (300), Interfaces (200)
- ALWAYS score complexity after planning (≥7 requires approval)
- ALWAYS read related code before modifying

### During Development
- ALWAYS cache manager references in Start(), validate before use
- ALWAYS use `LogExtensions` for debug logging (`this.Log()`)
- ALWAYS handle null references gracefully
- ALWAYS follow the region structure (see file-standards.mdc)

### DOTween & Odin (Required Tools)
- ALWAYS use DOTween for animations instead of coroutines (fades, movements, scaling)
- ALWAYS kill DOTweens in OnDestroy: `DOTween.Kill(transform); DOTween.Kill(this);`
- ALWAYS use Odin `[FoldoutGroup("Debug")]` for debug section organization
- ALWAYS use Odin `[Button]` for testable methods in inspector
- ALWAYS use Odin `[Required]` for critical ScriptableObject references

### Game-Specific
- ALWAYS use `CubeCollisionManager` for collision resolution
- ALWAYS configure content via ScriptableObjects, not hardcoded values
- ALWAYS respect marker economy rules (regeneration vs grants)

### Completion
- ALWAYS run build validation before marking task complete
- ALWAYS execute tasks one at a time via Shrimp

## Approved Third-Party Tools

| Tool | Purpose | Required Import |
|------|---------|-----------------|
| DOTween Pro | Animations, tweens, sequences | `using DG.Tweening;` |
| Odin Inspector | Inspector enhancement, validation | `using Sirenix.OdinInspector;` |

**DOTween vs Coroutines:**
- DOTween: Visual animations (fade, move, scale, rotate, color)
- Coroutines: Async logic, waiting for conditions, frame delays

